# UI, Theme & Accessibility

## Purpose

Consistent look-and-feel from shared theme tokens, with accessible defaults.

## When Applied

Building or styling widgets/pages, or editing theme files under `lib/core/theme/`.

## Requirements

- Use existing theme tokens: `lib/core/theme/`, `app_colors.dart`, `sizes.dart`, `app_gradients.dart`, custom `ThemeData` extensions.
- Reuse shared widgets (`custom_snackbar`, `shimmer_widgets`, `app_search_bar`, `branded_pull_to_refresh`) before writing new ones.
- Respect readable contrast and ≥48dp touch targets.
- See [`docs/ui-theme-guide.md`](../../../docs/ui-theme-guide.md).

## Examples

- Loading state → reuse `shimmer_widgets`, not a custom spinner.
- Error/success toast → `custom_snackbar`.

## Anti-patterns

- Hard-coded hex colors or magic paddings instead of `AppColors`/`Sizes`.
- One-off `SnackBar`/loading widgets that duplicate shared ones.

## Common Mistakes

- Ignoring dark/appbar theme, so the widget looks off in one mode.
- Tiny tap targets or low-contrast text.
